nodecode-little-canary is a rewrite of hermes-labs-ai's hermes-labs-ai/little-canary:

  https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/little-canary
  commit 61855a940a66fb8319742756c3ff72c720a89160
  Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Hermes Labs (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the Hermes Agent plugin at integrations/hermes-agent -- its screening
pipeline, in Common Lisp. The structural family of injection shapes and their
weights, the baseline system prompt the canary model is given, the behavioural
reading of its answer, the PASS/FLAG/BLOCK/DEGRADED dispositions with a risk
score and the signals behind it, the fail-open rule (unexercised coverage
withholds nothing), and the gate that withdraws a turn's tool calls on a BLOCK
with a TTL. The canary is the same local Ollama model over the same /api/chat
wire, and the same "screened text only" rule keeps the conversation out of it.

Left out, and why: the Hermes hook points themselves -- pre_llm_call has no
Nodecode equivalent, so the screening is a tool the model calls and a /canary
command the operator types, rather than an automatic pass over every user turn;
the advisory-only mode and the second LLM judge (an opt-in provider the plugin
also bundles) because one threshold and one canary answer cover what the tool
is for; the plugin's optional JSONL audit log, which would write files the
platform does not need; and the OpenAI-compatible probe, since a keyed
third-party endpoint is a different product rather than this one. The plugin's
own copy of the runtime, its CLI and its demo are not carried over.
